BT 1 0 0 1 0 63 Tm 12 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Paper 152 formalized the ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Mirror Interface Principle) Tj /F1 9 Tf (: any computational agent constructing output for an external observer) Tj T* (renders from behind the interface, and the interface inverts the lateral axis. This paper extends the principle to human) Tj T* (biology. The human visual and motor systems contain at least three distinct interface inversions -- the eye's lens, the optic) Tj T* (chiasm, and the pyramidal decussation -- each performing a transformation between the internal representation and the) Tj T* (observable world. Consciousness, in the human case as in the computational case, sits ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (behind the glass) Tj /F1 9 Tf (. The glass) Tj T* (always inverts. This is not metaphor; it is anatomy.) Tj T* ET
